accTitle: Planner routing, evaluation, strategy-specific selection, and authorization
accDescr: PlannerRouter chooses a strategy. A planner searches and calls CandidateEvaluator to replay a proposed path, check feasibility, and calculate values. CandidateEvaluator does not choose a candidate. Candidate ordering and retention are implemented inside each strategy; there is no shared CandidateSelector. The resulting proposal remains separate from downstream authorization and grounding execution.

    ROUTE[PlannerRouter<br/>select strategy] --> PLAN[Selected PlanningStrategy]
    PLAN --> SEARCH[Strategy-specific search<br/>successor ranking, tree selection,<br/>branch pruning or linear extension]
    SEARCH --> EVAL[CandidateEvaluator<br/>replay + feasibility + score]
    EVAL --> SEARCH
    SEARCH --> RETAIN[Strategy-specific candidate<br/>ordering and retention]
    RETAIN --> PROPOSAL[PlanCandidate proposal(s)]
    PROPOSAL --> AUTH[Downstream authorization<br/>and dispatch]
    AUTH --> EXEC[Grounding execution]
